  <section class="roof-painting-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h2">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Your Questions Answered</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" id="faq-h2">Roof Painting Kilkenny — FAQs</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" role="list">

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q1">How long does roof painting last in Kilkenny?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">A professionally applied roof coating in Kilkenny typically lasts 10–15 years, depending on the coating product used, the condition of the tiles beforehand, and how well the roof was prepared. Kilkenny's wet Atlantic climate means preparation — especially thorough cleaning and biocide treatment — is critical to longevity. We only use proven, weather-resistant coatings suited to the Irish climate.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q2">Is roof painting worth it in Ireland?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">Yes, for most homes it is excellent value. A roof paint or coating seals porous tiles, prevents moss and algae regrowth, stops water ingress, and dramatically improves kerb appeal — all for a fraction of the cost of a full roof replacement. In the Kilkenny climate, where moss and lichen spread quickly on north-facing roof slopes, regular coating can add years to the life of an existing roof.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q3">Do you need to clean the roof before painting?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">Absolutely. Cleaning is the single most important step. We pressure-wash the entire roof surface to remove moss, lichen, dirt, and loose material, then apply a biocide treatment to kill any remaining biological growth at the root. Painting over a dirty or mossy roof will cause the coating to fail prematurely. We never skip this stage.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q4">What types of roofs can you paint?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">We paint concrete and clay roof tiles, natural slate, fibre cement slates, and some flat-roof surfaces. Each material requires a specific primer or coating for proper adhesion. During our free survey we'll assess your roof type and recommend the most suitable product. We do not paint roofs in a structural condition that would be unsafe to walk.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q5">How much does roof painting cost in Kilkenny?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">Roof painting costs vary based on roof size, pitch, accessibility, current condition, and the product specified. As a rough guide, a typical semi-detached house in Kilkenny might range from €800 to €2,500+, while larger detached homes will be higher. We provide fully itemised free quotes with no hidden extras — contact us for an accurate price for your property.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q6">How long does the job take?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">Most domestic roof painting projects in Kilkenny take 2–4 days to complete: one day for cleaning and preparation, a drying/settling period, and then one to two days for coating application. Larger or more complex roofs may take longer. We work efficiently to minimise disruption and always keep you updated on progress.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q7">Will roof painting stop leaks?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">A roof coating can seal minor porosity in tiles and help reduce water ingress through degraded tile surfaces. However, it is not a substitute for structural repairs such as replacing cracked tiles, re-pointing ridge tiles, or fixing flashing. Before we paint, we always inspect for and flag any underlying repairs needed — and we can carry out re-pointing of ridge tiles as part of the job.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q8">What colours can I choose for my roof?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">We offer a range of colours suitable for roof tiles, including terracotta, charcoal, slate grey, dark brown, and tile red. The available palette depends on the coating product best suited to your roof type. We bring colour samples to your free quote appointment so you can see the options in natural light before committing.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q9">Do you re-point ridge tiles as part of roof painting?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">Yes. Re-pointing cracked or crumbling ridge tile mortar is highly recommended before coating, as failed pointing allows water ingress and can cause ridge tiles to become loose. We can include ridge tile re-pointing as part of your full roof painting package in Kilkenny, giving you a complete, weatherproof finish in one visit.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q10">Are you insured and experienced in working at height?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">Yes. Kilkenny County Painters carry full public liability insurance, and our team is experienced in working safely at height on domestic roofs. We use appropriate access equipment for each job — ladders, scaffold towers, or scaffolding for larger roofs — in line with safe working practices.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q11">Do you serve areas outside Kilkenny city?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">Yes. We cover the whole of County Kilkenny including Thomastown, Callan, Castlecomer, Graiguenamanagh, Urlingford, Bennetsbridge, Freshford, Piltown, Mullinavat, and surrounding townlands. If you're unsure whether we cover your area, just give us a call and we'll let you know straight away.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="faq-item__q" id="faq-q12">How do I get a quote for roof painting in Kilkenny?</h3>
          <p class="faq-item__a">Getting a quote is simple and completely free. Call us on <a href="tel:+353873566934" style="color:var(--pd-accent);font-weight:700;">+353 87 356 6934</a>, email <a href="mailto:kilkennycountypainter@gmail.com" style="color:var(--pd-accent);font-weight:700;">kilkennycountypainter@gmail.com</a>, or fill out the contact form on this page. We'll arrange a convenient time to visit your property, assess the roof, and provide a written, no-obligation quote — usually within 48 hours.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

